      "height": 1836,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
      "artist": "Jidanni",
      "description": "Here the Sun is seen covering much more of the sky than usual at sunrise, almost like a nuclear explosion, due to ice clouds. Zao Keng, Dongshi District, Taichung City, (central) Taiwan.\nIn the center of the image is 東卯山 Dongmao Mtn. At right is 白毛山 Baimao shan. And the farthest in back, from left to right, is 白姑大山 Baigu Mountain, 基隆山 Jilong Shan, 九仙山 Jiuxian Shan.\nIn the foreground is a banana plantation.\n(Try setting Image Gamma to 18 to see full \"nuclear\" effect.)\nSee also:\n\nFile:- panoramio (2441).jpg\nFile:7ème ciel 01.jpg",
      "dateCreated": "17 June 2020 (according to <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exif\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Exif\">Exif</a></span> data)",
